<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad Diler Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad Diler Khan was an Afghan officer in Mughal service who founded the small state of Kurwai in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1713. He received a territory near the Betwa river, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidisha">Vidisha</a>, and his descendants ruled it as nawabs, later under British paramountcy, until the state joined independent India after 1947.</p></div>
